  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantLeaseholdsThatHaveBeenAcquiredOrGivenAssignedOrSurrenderedTextBlock id="f-36" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;4. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantLeaseholdsThatHaveBeenAcquiredOrGivenAssignedOrSurrenderedTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantExtensionOrReductionOfTransmissionOrDistributionSystemTextBlock id="f-37" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;5. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%;text-decoration:underline"&gt;Docket Numbers: CP26-82-000, CP26-87-000, and CP18-513-000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;On February 3, 2026, Cheniere Corpus Christi Pipeline, L.P. (&#8220;CCPL&#8221;) filed an application (&#8220;February Application&#8221;) with the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (&#8220;FERC&#8221;) (Docket No. CP26-87-000) for a certificate of public convenience and necessity pursuant to Section 7(c) of the Natural Gas Act (&#8220;7(c) Certificate&#8221;) to construct, own, operate, and maintain new natural gas pipeline facilities comprised of a 42-inch-diameter, approximately 25.8-mile-long natural gas pipeline loop, compression and metering facilities, and associated appurtenant facilities (&#8220;CCPL Expansion Project&#8221;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;Once authorized and constructed, the CCPL Expansion Project will increase gas delivery capacity from Sinton, Texas to both the existing Corpus Christi liquefied natural gas terminal (&#8220;CCL Terminal&#8221;) and a proposed expansion of the CCL Terminal (the &#8220;CCL Stage 4 Project&#8221;) by approximately 2.75 billion cubic feet per day.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;The February Application also included CCPL&#8217;s request for a limited amendment of its 7(c) Certificate granted in Docket No. CP18-513-000 for its Stage 3 Pipeline Project, to vacate the previously granted authorization for a 21-mile-long, 42-inch-diameter pipeline loop, and to reflect the changes in contracted capacity, costs, and rates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantExtensionOrReductionOfTransmissionOrDistributionSystemTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock id="f-38" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;6. See &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#0000ff;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;text-decoration:underline"&gt;&lt;a style="color:#0000ff;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;text-decoration:underline" href="wurl://docs.v1/doc:eba7596413c6423f81826d36c8b92e92/sec:eba7596413c6423f81826d36c8b92e92_49"&gt;Note 5 - Guarantees&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock>
