  <ferc:ReportPeriod id="f-55" contextRef="c-1">Q2</ferc:ReportPeriod>
  <ferc:RespondentLegalName id="f-56" contextRef="c-1">Cheniere Corpus Christi Pipeline, LP</ferc:RespondentLegalName>
  <ferc:RespondentLegalName id="f-57" contextRef="c-1">Cheniere Corpus Christi Pipeline, LP</ferc:RespondentLegalName>
  <ferc:AttestationDate id="f-58" contextRef="c-1">2026-08-28</ferc:AttestationDate>
  <ferc:ReportYear id="f-59" contextRef="c-1" decimals="0" unitRef="u-1">2026</ferc:ReportYear>
  <ferc:ReportPeriod id="f-60" contextRef="c-1">Q2</ferc:ReportPeriod>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-61" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;NOTE 1&#8212;NATURE OF OPERATIONS AND BASIS OF PRESENTATION&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Cheniere Corpus Christi Pipeline, L.P. (&#8220;CCP&#8221;), a Delaware limited partnership, is a Houston-based partnership with one general partner, Corpus Christi Pipeline GP, LLC (&#8220;CCP GP&#8221;), and one limited partner, Cheniere Corpus Christi Holdings, LLC (&#8220;CCH&#8221;), both of which are indirect subsidiaries of Cheniere Energy, Inc. (&#8220;Cheniere&#8221;). Unless the context requires otherwise, references to &#8220;we,&#8221; &#8220;us&#8221; and &#8220;our&#8221; refer to CCP.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;We own an approximately 21-mile natural gas supply pipeline (the &#8220;Corpus Christi Pipeline&#8221;) that interconnects a natural gas liquefaction and export facility near Corpus Christi, Texas (the &#8220;Corpus Christi LNG terminal&#8221;), owned by Corpus Christi Liquefaction, LLC (&#8220;CCL&#8221;), a subsidiary of CCH, with several interstate and intrastate natural gas pipelines. The Corpus Christi Pipeline is designed to transport up to 2.75 billion cubic feet per day (&#8220;Bcf/d&#8221;) of feed gas and has contracted firm transportation capacity through existing firm pipeline transportation and other agreements with CCL. Our transactions with associated companies, as referenced throughout these notes, are with subsidiaries of Cheniere.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Our cash needs are funded through contributions received from our limited partner and, in the absence of legal or contractual restrictions, we typically distribute all of our net cash inflows to our limited partner. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Basis of Presentation &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The accompanying Financial Statements of CCP have been prepared in accordance with the accounting regulations of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (&#8220;FERC&#8221;), as set forth in the applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which are a comprehensive basis of accounting other than U.S. generally accepted accounting principles (&#8220;GAAP&#8221;). The most significant differences between GAAP and the comprehensive basis of accounting applied in these Financial Statements are our election to include an income tax provision herein, as well as classification of certain accounts on our Comparative Balance Sheet, Statement of Income and Statement of Cash Flows. These interim Financial Statements do not include all of the information and footnotes required by FERC for complete financial statements and should be read in conjunction with the Financial Statements and accompanying notes included in our FERC Form No. 2 for the year ended December 31, 2025. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;We are a disregarded entity for federal, state and local income tax purposes.&#160;Our taxable income or loss, which may vary substantially from the net income or loss reported on our Statement of Income, is included in the consolidated tax return of Cheniere.&#160;The provision for income taxes, taxes payable and deferred income tax balances have been recorded as if we had filed all tax returns on a separate return basis from Cheniere. Any current tax liability calculated on a separate return basis is deemed to be settled by a non-cash equity contribution from Cheniere which represents non-cash financing activity, as disclosed in &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#0000ff;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;text-decoration:underline"&gt;&lt;a style="color:#0000ff;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;text-decoration:underline" href="#ieba7596413c6423f81826d36c8b92e92_46"&gt;Note 4&#8212;Supplemental Cash Flow Information&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;. Tax elections under a separate return basis may differ from tax elections taken on the consolidated federal income tax return of Cheniere.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Results of operations for the three and six months ended June 30, 2026 are not necessarily indicative of the results of operations that will be realized for the year ending December 31, 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Management has evaluated subsequent events through August&#160;28, 2026, the date the Financial Statements were available to be issued.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;NOTE 2&#8212;NET UTILITY PLANT&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Net utility plant consisted of the following (in thousands):&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:57.318%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.532%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:18.958%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.532%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:18.960%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:center;ve